# Otto ↔ Claude bridge + Generator–Relay–Applier

A secret-gated seam between **Otto** (Audos: research + orchestration, no prod access), **Cursor**
(Otto's code generator, no prod/repo access), **Claude Code** (rolec checkout + prod Supabase +
gh — the only wired applier), and **Cowork-Claude** (direct prod Supabase read/write; cannot reach
the bus). **Proven end-to-end 2026-08-22:** 3 ES→IE facts promoted to `requirement_items` (pending),
append-only, zero reviewed rows touched, nothing served.

## Environments (the split is real — it forces the pattern)

| | Otto (Audos) | Cursor (Otto→delegation) | Claude Code | Cowork |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Research / LLM codegen | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Reach `audos.com` bus | ✅ | — | ✅ | ❌ (egress-blocked) |
| rolec repo + gh | ❌ | ❌ (not wired) | ✅ | read-only via device bridge |
| Prod Supabase write | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ (MCP) |

Cursor is **not** wired to prod/repo, and shouldn't be given write access. So it **generates**;
a wired agent **applies**; Cowork **verifies**.

## When to use vs. NOT

- **Bridge / Generator–Relay–Applier:** Otto-*originated* research not in the repo, or code/SQL to
  be generated by Cursor's fleet.
- **NOT the bridge:** a batch already committed to rolec → Claude Code stages/promotes it directly.

## The bus contract

- URL `https://audos.com/api/hooks/execute/workspace-776786/otto-claude-bridge`
- `push {direction, kind, payload, source?}` → `{ok,id}` · `pull {direction, sinceId?}` → `{ok,rows}`
  (pending only, `id>sinceId`) · `ack {ids:[…]}` → `{ok,updated}`. Directions `otto_to_claude`,
  `claude_to_otto`. `kind` ∈ `["message","record","manifest"]` (`"receipt"` is rejected 400).
- Secret in `x-hook-secret` header; Claude Code reads `~/.otto-bridge-secret`. Never in a payload.
- **Otto's bus tools are context-dependent** (a fresh Audos chat can lack `test_server_function`).
  For fact transport, prefer Claude Code as the bus endpoint.

## THE PROVEN LOOP — Generator → Relay → Applier → Verify (per promotion unit)

1. **Claude Code builds a read-only CONTEXT BUNDLE** (`.md`): target schema + natural upsert key,
   the mapping rules (incl. `resolve_pillar`), a per-fact JSON snapshot with `__promote:true/false`,
   the live rows for the concept (the append-only tripwires), the rules, and the OUTPUT CONTRACT.
2. **Otto delegates the bundle to Cursor.** Cursor returns **DECISIONS** — a reconciliation with a
   chosen **title per fact** (reviewable markdown). *Cursor decides; it does not emit raw SQL.*
3. **Cowork verifies the decisions** against prod: the chosen titles must not collide with any live
   `(country_code, purpose, title)` (exact + fuzzy). Titles are the dedup key.
4. **Claude Code (thin applier)** turns the verified decisions into SQL via the repo's own
   derivation, **dry-runs** (`BEGIN … ROLLBACK`; before/after count; pre-existing fingerprint), then
   applies **promote-to-PENDING**. Use `INSERT … SELECT` from `otto_staging` for long `fact_text`
   (no transcription drift).
5. **Cowork verifies the applied result** against prod (the recipe below).

**Four rules that made it work (do not skip):**
1. **Cursor decides, doesn't SQL** — judgment is its strength; SQL stays with the wired agent.
2. **The wired applier owns SQL + dry-run + apply** — it knows the exact id/mapping derivation.
3. **Cowork verifies independently** via direct prod read — never the executor.
4. **Relay artifacts as FILES, not pasted text** — paste corrupts; files arrive intact.

## Key mechanics

- **Grain:** `promote()` emits one row per *topic*, but the live corpus is *fact-grained*. To
  promote N specific facts, generate **N per-fact rows with per-fact titles**.
- **Deterministic id:** `uuid5(a1c9e349-0000-4000-8000-000000000001, "<country_code>|<purpose>|<title>")`
  — the `seed_requirements.py:build_payloads` format, reused at `executor.py:477`. Re-derivation
  converges with the YAML seeder (no duplicate rows). Cowork can't compute this reliably (needs the
  exact key format) — the wired applier does.
- **Natural upsert key `(country_code, purpose, title)`.** `create_requirement_item` upserts and
  **rewrites description/severity/owner/citations on collision** → NEVER emit a row whose key
  matches a reviewed row. Append-only.
- **Titles follow the live corpus** — two families in IE: `"Critical Skills Permit – …"` (en-dash),
  `"Ireland — …"` (em-dash). A one-character dash difference is a different row.

## Verification recipe (Cowork, read-only, after apply)

- **before → after count** = +N.
- **md5 fingerprint** over the untouched rows must be **unchanged** — the strongest proof no reviewed
  row was overwritten. Compute it with the **Canonical integrity fingerprint** SQL below — the single
  exact expression both applier and verifier use. Do NOT hand-roll a different column set or separator:
  a divergent formula yields an incomparable hash (the isd_irp false-mismatch, and the tripwire-composite
  drift on revenue_rpn — same data, different formula, different number).
- the **tripwire** rows (specific `verified`/reviewed rows) unchanged — check with the SAME canonical
  expression restricted to the tripwire ids, or by direct content diff.
- **`expert_verified` count = 0** — nothing over-claimed.
- the **N new rows** present, all `review_status='pending'`, correct pillar/purpose/verification_status.

## Canonical integrity fingerprint (applier AND verifier compute THIS EXACT SQL)

The append-only cross-check only works if both sides hash identically. Use this verbatim, over the
target country, EXCLUDING every id touched this run (new inserts + any deliberately-updated rows):

```sql
SELECT md5(string_agg(
  id||'|'||title||'|'||coalesce(description,'')||'|'||coalesce(pillar,'')||'|'||
  coalesce(purpose,'')||'|'||coalesce(review_status,'')||'|'||coalesce(verification_status,''),
  '~' ORDER BY id))
FROM public.requirement_items
WHERE country_code = '<COUNTRY>'
  AND id <> ALL (ARRAY[ <every id changed this run, as text> ]);
```

- The **applier** computes it in the dry-run (before) and after apply over the SAME excluded set — the
  two must be identical (proves the run touched nothing else).
- **Cowork** recomputes the identical expression independently; its value MUST equal the applier's.
  Divergence -> stop (formula drift or a concurrent write), do not sign off.
- The applier MUST report its id-exclusion list so the verifier reproduces the set exactly.

## Governance (hard)

- **Promote-to-PENDING only.** Rows land `review_status='pending'` → not served
  (`requirements_builder` returns approved only). The flip to served/approved on immigration/tax/
  legal content is the **human lawyer gate at `/admin/countries`** — never auto-serve.
- **Append-only; honor pillar** (`TAX→EMPLOYMENT`, refuse unknown/conflicting); never overwrite a
  reviewed row.
- After apply, **mark the promoted staged facts** (`otto_staging … status new→promoted`) so a re-run
  doesn't redo them.

## Roles

- **Otto** — research + orchestrate + relay (`cursor_delegation`, bus). Research is its heavy lift.
- **Cursor** — generator: reconciliation + title decisions (reviewable). No prod/repo access.
- **Claude Code** — wired applier: context bundle + SQL + dry-run + promote-to-pending.
- **Cowork** — independent verifier + context/skill/task author. Reaches prod, not the bus.
- **Human** — every 🔴 gate: serve-to-mover, code merge to main, lawyer review.
